// remote_reachability_registry_test.go — Task 4 of the G80 158-method
// classification pass (docs/adr-087-remote-storage-deletion-pass.md).
//
// remoteUnsupportedAllowlist (remote_unsupported_completeness_test.go)
// answers "is this a legitimate, permanent stub" — statusIntentional/
// statusUnverified/statusKnownGap. It says nothing about whether the stub is
// reachable by a real deployment path. That second question is what Wave 0
// individually answered for only 13 of what was then believed to be 88 (later
// 171, then 183) structurally-stub methods — the other 158 sat unclassified
// on this axis until this pass. Unclassified dead code becomes live code
// without re-review; this codebase has a concrete instance of exactly that
// (RequireNodeCredentialOrPermission's node arm, ADR-085). This registry
// closes the gap: every currently-registered RemoteStorage stub method has an
// entry here, and TestEveryStructuralStubHasReachabilityVerdict below fails
// the build the moment a NEW stub-shaped method is added without one — same
// discipline as remote_unsupported_completeness_test.go's own guard, and the
// same "no third state, no silent additions" shape as scripts/ci-test-legs.sh's
// C5 ratchet.
//
// A SEPARATE registry rather than a new field on remoteUnsupportedEntry:
// adding a field to that struct would require touching every one of its ~183
// existing positional struct-literal call sites across ~20 files for a
// concern those entries were never about. This registry is purpose-built,
// additive, and touches nothing else.
package store

import (
	"sort"
	"testing"
)

// reachabilityStatus classifies whether a structurally-stub RemoteStorage
// method is actually reachable by a real storage.type: remote deployment —
// orthogonal to remoteUnsupportedStatus (which classifies stub legitimacy).
type reachabilityStatus int

const (
	// reachabilityLive means a real CLI command reaches this method,
	// unguarded by any of the three established remote/local dual-path
	// idioms (NewRemoteClient/ResolveRemote/IsClientMode family), under a
	// hard stub. A broken (or, more rarely, silently-wrong) feature — see
	// the entry's reason for the specific command and failure mode.
	reachabilityLive reachabilityStatus = iota
	// reachabilityDead means every path that could reach this method is
	// either guarded (a sibling raw-HTTP passthrough always wins first),
	// server-only (ADR-083: no server process can boot with storage.type:
	// remote), or has no caller at all.
	reachabilityDead
	// reachabilityUnresolved means neither could be established with the
	// evidence available. Kept, not deleted, not guessed — the entry's
	// reason names what evidence would settle it.
	reachabilityUnresolved
)

type reachabilityEntry struct {
	status reachabilityStatus
	reason string
}

